gned up at brittany's request  we had two immediate goals in mind  on july 14th i announced that we were  going to move aggressively  and expeditiously  to  remove mr spears  as conservator or i should say suspend  mr spears as conservator  we filed our petition to suspend him  on july 26th  the court granted our petition and  suspended him on september 29th  and then part two of our assignment was  termination of the conservatorship and  we achieved that on november 12th those  were the two primary goals here and we  achieved both of them and i'm very proud  of that and britney is very happy about  that i was asked about the legislation i  think you asked about  as i understand it and i think this is  operative you can correct me if i'm  wrong legislation inspired by britney's  case was introduced  into the california legislature i  believe today is that correct  assembly  the assembly will substantially change  excuse me the bill will substantially  change as i understand it the probate  conservatorship system making it harder  initially for judges to establish  conservatorships in the first place  and easier for people to  get out of conservatorships the bill  also requires the court to appoint  counsel and schedule a hearing  immediately if a person wishes to  terminate their his or her  conservatorship  next the bill as i understand it also  requires conservators to consult and  make decisions aligned with the  conservatives communicated wishes which  actually  is part of the conservators handbook now  but i believe it will be codified into  law pursuant to this bill  one of the first things i learned as a  commercial litigator coming into the  space of probate law as judge penny  pointed out at the first hearing i  attended on july 14  is what a conservator is supposed to do  is act in the best interests of the  conservancy  and that's something i believe this bill  is going to address as well i think it's  fair to say that if this law had been  enacted or on the books 13 years ago  britney might not have been conserved in  the first place or there might have been  a different type of  uh lps conservatorship i believe is the  proper terminology which is a short-term  uh much more short-term short-term  conservatorship  what conservatives are also supposed to  do  what courts are supposed to do is look  at the least restrictive needs  and query whether that happens here as  well i'm not being critical of the court  but i believe that's something the  system is going to address pursuant to  this bill  so that's my take on the legislation we  think it makes sense we support it  we're proud that brittany shines a light  on some of the problems systemically as  i've said before from california to new  york and i think i've summarized the  bill and we expect it to work its way  through the legislation
 

